How to Bypass Login Screen and Enable Full Data Editing

To make this app load straight into the dashboard without the login screen and enable full data editing, here are the specific code adjustments you need to make:

1. Comment Out the Login Screen

In the HTML section, find the login screen div and comment it out:

```html
<!-- Login Screen - Commented out for auto-login
<div id="login-screen">
    ... (all login content)
</div>
-->
```

2. Auto-Login on Page Load

Add this to the JavaScript initialization (around line 1210, in the initApp() function):

```javascript
function initApp() {
    console.log("Initializing EcoManager Pro...");
    
    db.init();
    auditLog.init();
    
    // === AUTO-LOGIN: Bypass login screen ===
    // Set user as Admin with full permissions
    currentUser.role = 'admin';
    currentUser.name = 'System Administrator';
    currentUser.permissions = ['all'];
    
    // Update UI to show admin role
    document.getElementById('currentUserRole').textContent = 'System Administrator';
    document.getElementById('currentUserRole').className = 'badge bg-danger text-dark mt-1';
    
    // Hide login screen immediately
    const loginScreen = document.getElementById('login-screen');
    if (loginScreen) {
        loginScreen.style.display = 'none';
        loginScreen.style.opacity = '0';
    }
    
    // Show welcome message
    showToast('Welcome', 'Logged in as System Administrator (Full Access)', 'success');
    
    // Initialize UI components
    loadProjectSelects();
    // ... rest of initApp
}
```

3. Enable Full Editing Permissions

The user roles and permissions are defined in the userRoles object. For full editing ability, you need to ensure the 'admin' role has 'all' permissions:

```javascript
const userRoles = {
    // ... other roles
    admin: {
        name: 'System Administrator',
        permissions: ['all'],  // This gives full access
        color: 'danger'
    }
};
```

4. Quick Fix: Direct Login Function Call

Alternatively, you can call the login function directly on page load with admin credentials:

```javascript
// Add this at the bottom of the script, outside any function
window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    // Auto-login as admin
    document.getElementById('userRole').value = 'admin';
    document.getElementById('demoPassword').value = 'council123';
    login();
});
```

5. Complete Modified initApp Function

Here's the complete modified initApp() function with all the necessary changes:

```javascript
function initApp() {
    console.log("Initializing EcoManager Pro...");
    
    db.init();
    auditLog.init();
    
    // ===== AUTO-LOGIN: Bypass login screen =====
    currentUser.role = 'admin';
    currentUser.name = 'System Administrator';
    currentUser.permissions = ['all'];
    
    // Update UI
    const userRoleBadge = document.getElementById('currentUserRole');
    if (userRoleBadge) {
        userRoleBadge.textContent = 'System Administrator';
        userRoleBadge.className = 'badge bg-danger text-dark mt-1';
    }
    
    // Hide login screen
    const loginScreen = document.getElementById('login-screen');
    if (loginScreen) {
        loginScreen.style.display = 'none';
        loginScreen.style.opacity = '0';
    }
    
    // Log the auto-login
    auditLog.log('USER_AUTO_LOGIN', { role: 'admin' });
    
    // Initialize UI components
    loadProjectSelects();
    initApiKeyManagement();
    setupViewToggle();
    setupHealthScorePreview();
    setupHealthChartControls();
    setupWeatherLocationSelector();
    
    // Load dashboard data
    setTimeout(function() {
        loadDashboard();
        loadDataSummary();
        
        setTimeout(function() {
            loadCharts();
            loadHealthChart();
            loadWeatherData();
        }, 200);
    }, 100);
    
    // User onboarding
    userOnboarding.showTooltips();
    
    // Initialize tooltips
    var tooltipTriggerList = [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-bs-toggle="tooltip"]'));
    var tooltipList = tooltipTriggerList.map(function (tooltipTriggerEl) {
        return new bootstrap.Tooltip(tooltipTriggerEl);
    });

    fixTableScrolling();
    console.log("EcoManager Pro initialized successfully!");
}
```

6. Comment Out the Login HTML

Find this section in the HTML and comment it out (around line 570):

```html
<!-- ===== LOGIN SCREEN - COMMENTED OUT FOR AUTO-LOGIN =====
<div id="login-screen">
    <div class="login-container">
        ... (all login HTML content)
    </div>
</div>
-->
```

Summary of Changes

Change Location What to Do
Comment out login screen HTML (~line 570) Wrap entire #login-screen div in <!-- -->
Auto-login as admin initApp() function (~line 1210) Set currentUser.role = 'admin' and hide login screen
Update user badge Same location Update the displayed role name
Ensure full permissions userRoles object Admin role already has ['all'] permissions

Testing

After making these changes:

1. The app should load directly to the dashboard
2. You should see "System Administrator" as your role
3. All buttons, forms, and edit functions should be enabled
4. You should be able to create, edit, and delete projects, assessments, species, and maintenance items

This approach gives you full administrative access without needing to go through the login screen.
